  "significance": 7,
  "status": "preprint",
  "summary": "LHAASO saw photons up to 3.7 PeV from Cygnus X-3, and the spectrum shows no sharp cutoff that photon decay would cause if light speed varied with energy. That sets the second-order Lorentz violation scale above 10^-2 Planck mass. It covers only superluminal scenarios and one flaring source, and assumes a hard intrinsic spectrum.",
  "tags": [
    "Lorentz invariance",
    "gamma rays",
    "LHAASO"
  ],
  "title": "Constraints on Lorentz Invariance Violation from PeV Gamma Rays of Cygnus X-3 Observed by LHAASO",
